  'guide.telegram.chatsTitle': 'Private chats and groups',
  'guide.telegram.chatsDesc': 'In a private chat the bot answers every message. In a group — only a reply to its own message or a message that starts with the persona’s trigger word (trigger_words in the YAML). You can send photos — the persona will look at them; the Telegram bot does not handle voice messages, voice lives in the console web chat.',
  'guide.console.personaTitle': 'Create a persona',
  'guide.console.personaDesc': 'Personas → «+ Create persona». Only the name is required — the id is made up for you. Config fields on the left, the live YAML on the right. You can paste a ready YAML or save a draft. The persona appears in the web chat right away, no restart; for Telegram add its <ID>_BOT_TOKEN to .env and restart the bot.',
  'guide.console.apiTitle': 'Providers: API',
  'guide.console.apiDesc': 'Settings → «Provider keys»: paste a service key and press «Add». Several keys for one service rotate: when one hits its limit, the persona takes the next. Primary and fallback provider, a custom model and per-task assignment for a specific persona — Chat → Dossier → «Settings».',
  'guide.console.webTitle': 'Providers: web chats',
  'guide.console.webDesc': 'No API keys: answers come from site chats in the bot’s Chrome window — you must be logged in there. Tick the sites under «Web chats as providers», «Check» sends a test message; enabled ones are tried in order. The limit is 40 messages an hour, adjustable in the persona dossier. Got a captcha — tell the bot:',
  'guide.console.ollamaTitle': 'Providers: Ollama',
  'guide.console.ollamaDesc': 'A model right on your computer: free and unlimited, but slower and simpler. Install Ollama and pull a model, keep the server address in the local provider row in Settings and press «Check availability» — the status tells whether the server is up and the model is there.',
